# CQ-C6 — For ANY node, what is its provenance and current review status?
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# I2 FIX (2026-07-08): the previous query answered PRIMARY UNITS only (nodes that carry
# their own reviewStatus + hasProvenance = the 21 Obligations). Per the Phase-4 targeting,
# Condition/Exception do NOT carry their own provenance/review — they INHERIT it from their
# parent Obligation/Right (reached via gdprkg:appliesIf / gdprkg:hasException). This version
# adds a UNION branch that resolves a Condition/Exception's provenance/status THROUGH its
# parent and labels each row ?mode = "direct" | "inherited", so the query answers "for ANY
# node", not just primary units.
# Expected over art13.ttl: 21 "direct" rows (one per Obligation) PLUS "inherited" rows for
# every Condition/Exception resolved through each parent it attaches to VIA ANY OF THE THREE
# parent relations (appliesIf, hasException, notApplicableIf — the third added 2026-09-06); e.g. the single
# 13(4) Exception resolves via all 21 obligations → 21 inherited rows; each Condition via
# the obligations whose appliesIf reaches it). Every grounded node's provenance is now
# resolvable; no grounded node is left without a provenance/status answer.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ENCODING FIX (2026-09-06) — gdprkg:notApplicableIf ADDED to the inherited parent path.
#
# THIS IS NOT A WIDENING OF THE QUESTION. The frozen competency question and its frozen
# probe were ALREADY broader than this query's encoding, and the encoding was the thing
# out of step. Verbatim from methodology/competency_questions.json (UNCHANGED by this fix):
#
#   question: "For any node, what is its provenance and current review status?"
#   probe:    "Provenance/review layer present from the start (provenance + reviewStatus
#              required on primary normative units; Condition/Exception inherit via parent)."
#
# The question says ANY node. The probe says Condition/Exception "inherit via parent" and
# names NO properties. This query hard-coded TWO of the three relations that can make a node
# a parent — appliesIf and hasException — and silently omitted the third, notApplicableIf.
# That was an omission in the ENCODING, not a boundary of the QUESTION.
#
# WHAT THIS RESOLVES: EXEC-9. ex:cond-46-1-adequacy-decision-exists — the Article 45(3)
# adequacy gate, attached to the 46(1) Permission by notApplicableIf ALONE — had NO
# provenance path under this query, and it was the ONLY node in the whole graph in that
# position. It now resolves. Measured: Condition/Exception nodes with no provenance answer
# 1 -> 0; inherited rows 238 -> 262 (+23 Work-Order-F Art-14 edges, +1 the Art-46 gate).
#
# NOTE WHAT WAS **NOT** DONE. CQ-A3 has the same blind spot and was DELIBERATELY LEFT ALONE
# (Zied, 2026-09-06, option B): its frozen PROBE names "APPLIES_IF edges" explicitly, so
# whether its question governs its probe is a live call and was not resolved by fiat. CQ-A3
# therefore still reports the Article-13 side only (112, not 135) and that stays a RECORDED
# NON-COVERAGE. competency_questions.json was not edited for either query.
#
# SEQUENCING, deliberate: this fix was held back from the Work Order F commit so that a
# frozen query is not seen to change in the same breath as the model change whose numbers
# depended on it. The model landed and was certified first; this stands on its own.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PREFIX gdprkg: <https://w3id.org/gdprkg#>
PREFIX prov:   <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#>
SELECT ?node ?mode ?status ?record ?activity ?agent
WHERE {
  {
    # direct: primary normative units (Obligation/Right/LegalBasis/Consent) carry their own
    ?node gdprkg:reviewStatus ?status ;
          gdprkg:hasProvenance ?record .
    BIND("direct" AS ?mode)
  }
  UNION
  {
    # inherited: a Condition/Exception resolves provenance/status via its parent norm.
    # gdprkg:notApplicableIf ADDED 2026-09-06 (Zied's decision, option B) — see the
    # ENCODING FIX note in this file's header.
    ?node a ?t .
    FILTER(?t IN (gdprkg:Condition, gdprkg:Exception))
    ?parent (gdprkg:appliesIf|gdprkg:hasException|gdprkg:notApplicableIf) ?node ;
            gdprkg:reviewStatus ?status ;
            gdprkg:hasProvenance ?record .
    BIND("inherited" AS ?mode)
  }
  OPTIONAL { ?record prov:wasGeneratedBy ?activity ; prov:wasAttributedTo ?agent }
}
ORDER BY ?mode ?node
